    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nI do not know if this is possible, but I have turned off cursor animations because I noticed it slowed down my movement when using [lightspeed.nvim](https://github.com/ggandor/lightspeed.nvim). I'd have to wait for the animation to finish before I could do actions at the desired cursor location.\r\n\r\nHowever I also have scrolloff turned on and if I move the cursor to somewhere near the bottom or top of my screen I have to wait again for the animation to finish before my cursor is in the proper spot because it triggers a vertical scroll event where I want animations turned on. So basically I'm wondering if it's possible to add something to turn off vertical animations _only_ caused by scrolloff (probably a stretch).\r\n\r\nAlternatively, if there was support for turning off certain animations runtime vs config time, I could change my configs so that way everytime I trigger lightspeed I turn off all mini.animate animations and then turn them back on afterwards.\r\n\r\nThank you!",
    "closed_at": "2023-06-13T01:47:39Z",
